# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_evaluate_honesty.py" "EVALUATE HONESTY GATE: PASS" "evaluate.py honesty: content-free + never-crash N/A + no overclaim/fragile number (TRY-BEFORE-YOU-BUY sales artifact)" "evaluate.py is the try-before-you-buy artifact a prospect runs on THEIR repo, so honesty is existential. This locks three properties END-TO-END ON REAL CRAFTED GIT REPOS (the existing test_evaluate*.py feed only SYNTHETIC analyze() results and never exercise the real git path): (1) CONTENT-FREE (cardinal) -- a whole-tool run on a repo carrying a secret in EVERY file body AND EVERY commit message leaks neither into stdout/stderr/--out report (evaluate.py reads paths + 'git log --name-only' ONLY). (2) NEVER-CRASH + HONEST N/A -- an empty (0-commit) repo, a non-git directory, a single-file repo, and a tiny flat repo each report an honest N/A and exit 0 instead of a Python stack trace; this regression-locks the real crash this gate's PR fixed (the shared engine's random-baseline sampling raised ValueError on <2 files-with-history; evaluate.py now pre-detects a degenerate repo content-free and reports N/A, without touching the shared backtest_cochange module). (3) HONEST CLAIMS / no fragile number / exit-code contract -- the report ALWAYS prints the 'does NOT prove rework-hours-saved' disclaimer + the content-free claim, NEVER uses overclaim words (guarantee/prevents bugs/correctness), and NEVER renders a fragile 'inf×' even on the applicable branch where a zero control baseline would divide-by-zero (now rendered as the true qualitative '≫'); exit 0 iff every applicable repo clears the bar. Hermetic + offline (throwaway git repos, isolated git config, no network, no Postgres)" "the customer-facing try-before-you-buy report stays honest and safe to run on any repo: it leaks no code body or commit message, never crashes or fabricates a number on a small/empty repo (it says N/A), never overclaims correctness or hours-saved, and its pass/fail exit code is trustworthy" 30
